TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Image 1"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Useful Links"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"No quantified mission requirements: spatial resolution, spectral bands, revisit time, coverage, data rate or mission lifetime are never specified, so the concept is not yet designable."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"No orbit, altitude, launch vehicle or payload sizing analysis; COEs/AOEs and launch specifics are only listed as future tasks, so space-segment feasibility is unsubstantiated."},{"where":"Image 1","issue":"Gantt legend states completed stages are gold and incomplete blue, but completed cells appear yellow; the red deadline line placement and Week 9 finish for STK design are inconsistent with the Week 10 finalisation note."},{"where":"Useful Links","issue":"References given as bare URLs without titles, authors or dates; in-text footnote numbering does not map to a single consistent reference list."}],"overall":"Attractive, well-written mission concept with a sound rationale and a plausible Gantt plan, but no quantitative requirements or real design analysis yet. Presentation is strong; references need formatting. Progress is essentially background research plus STK tutorials, so the technical evidence lags the narrative.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":32.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"Clear purpose (GBR bleaching monitoring), identified users (marine/conservation scientists), strong justification with statistics and four cited sources, plus an innovative sensing concept (seafloor colour change). Falls short of full marks because no quantified mission requirements (resolution, revisit, coverage, payload) or objectives are stated.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"In 2016, a bleaching killed 30 percent of the reef’s coral. In 2017, another 20 percent perished."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":18.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"A reasonably detailed Gantt chart and task-by-task descriptions covering launch, orbit, comms, EOL and STK give confidence the project is feasible. However, no contingencies or schedule slack/variation provision are given, and the link to the mission concept is only implicit, so it sits at the top of Adequate.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart. Detailed task descriptions can be found on the next page."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"**Strategies:** The goal is to brainstorm and research as many possible strategies for the satellite’s launch/orbit"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Only background reading and completion of four STK tutorials is reported; no design results, calculations, orbit/launch analysis or sensor trades are presented. This is minor work with no interpretation of results, matching the top of the Adequate band rather than Deficient, since a foundation has been laid.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"I have read the brief of Asner’s monitoring system in Hawaii, researched into how coral bleaching occurs and its severity, and also completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":16.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Well written, logical headings, clear prose and a legible, labelled Gantt chart; numbered footnotes match the reference list. Mark reduced because the source list is a raw 'Useful Links' block of bare URLs rather than a consistently formatted reference list, and the Gantt colour legend (gold/blue) does not match the chart shown.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Coral reefs, specifically the Great Barrier Reef, would immensely benefit from dedicated satellite monitoring."},{"where":"Useful Links","quote":"https://coralreefwatch.noaa.gov/satellite/publications/nim_skirving_reef_vulnerability.pdf"}]}]}
